167	## Edit 1.3 — `kDecNumDwSpecs` constant (NEW) next to the DecDwSpec struct
168	
169	Add a compile-time spec count right after the `DecDwSpec` struct closes (line
170	1967 `};`). It is the array bound everywhere a dW spec array is declared/passed.
171	
172	OLD:
173	```
174	    __nv_bfloat16* dYt;        // [Mpad, K] (transposed dY) — null unless active
175	    __nv_bfloat16* Xt;         // [Kin,  K] (transposed X)  — null unless active
176	    int64_t t_off;             // element offset of (dYt|Xt) base in the dW-T scratch
177	#endif
178	};
179	```
180	
181	NEW:
182	```
183	    __nv_bfloat16* dYt;        // [Mpad, K] (transposed dY) — null unless active
184	    __nv_bfloat16* Xt;         // [Kin,  K] (transposed X)  — null unless active
185	    int64_t t_off;             // element offset of (dYt|Xt) base in the dW-T scratch
186	#endif
187	};
188	
189	// Number of dW specs: 4 per layer (in_proj, out_proj, ff0, ff2) + 1 head.out.
190	//   = 4*L + 1  (= 9 at L=2, the original spec[9]; = 193 at the flagship L=48).
191	// This is the compile-time bound for EVERY DecDwSpec array (the DecTcSmem member,
192	// every spec[] signature/local, the dW phase loops, the bias prefix). At L=2 it
193	// is exactly 9 → the spec arrays + their stack/smem footprint are byte-identical.
194	constexpr int kDecNumDwSpecs = 4 * dec::kLayers + 1;
195	```
